Following the structure of Eq. (2), the FFNN-S is implemented as a one-step predictor.
It receives as inputs the state variables, C(t ― δt), the control inputs u[t―δt,t] (which are
constant over time intervals [t ― δt,t]), and time intervals, δt. When the time step δt is
constant it may drop from the FFNN-S inputs. Of note that δt might not be constant
