The ODEs are numerically integrated over time intervals [t ― δt,t]
from initial conditions, C(t ― dt) to the current concentrations, C(t).
The integration was done numerically with a Runge-Kutta 4th order method (RK4).
This is another fundamental difference to PINNs, as the hybrid semiparametric
approach requires integration whereas the PINN approach requires differentiation.
However, it is important to note that the discretization of the process to match sampling
time steps can impact the derivative approximation and overall solution accuracy, as
highlighted by Cruz-Bournazou et al. (2022). Comparing computed and measured
concentrations results in a data loss that is minimized during the training (further
described below).
