physics loss reduction is however not reflected in the data loss terms, which seem to
be relatively insensitive to the K/NWS ratio. It was concluded that a K/NWS =1 is
sufficient for achieving robust model convergence. Importantly, the computational cost
(CPU) escalates linearly with increasing K/NWS. Consequently, a ratio of 1 presents
an optimal balance between model accuracy and computational efficiency. For this
reason, K/NWS=1 was set in all tests performed in the present study.
